# BPE Cleaning Services, environment variables.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values. .env is git ignored, this file is not,
# so never put a real key below. Full walkthrough in docs/CABINET-RO.md.
#
# The site runs fine with none of these set: the cabinet shows "Not connected yet",
# traffic is not recorded, and the quote form still opens WhatsApp as before.

# Supabase project URL.
# Where: Supabase > Settings > API > Project URL.
# Public: the PUBLIC_ prefix means it is bundled into the browser, which is intended.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase anon key, used by the cabinet in the browser and by the blog pages for reads.
# Where: Supabase > Settings > API > Project API keys > anon public.
# Public: it is safe to ship. Every table it touches is behind row level security, and
# every policy asks whether the signed-in address is listed in admin_emails.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Supabase service role key, used only on the server by /api/track, /api/lead and /go/[code].
# Where: Supabase > Settings > API > Project API keys > service_role secret.
# SECRET: it bypasses row level security completely. Never prefix it with PUBLIC_, never
# commit it, never paste it into a client side file. On Vercel mark it as sensitive.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Salt for the daily visitor hash (day + IP + user agent + salt, no IP is ever stored).
# Where: invent one, a long random string, at least 32 characters.
# REQUIRED for unique visitor counts, and there is no default. Without it the hash is
# not produced at all: page views are still recorded, the visitor code is left empty and
# the cabinet counts no unique visitors. That is on purpose. The formula is public, so a
# salt everybody knows is the same as no salt, and it would let anyone holding a copy of
# the analytics table work the IP addresses back out. Better to lose a number.
# SECRET: keep it out of the repository, on Vercel mark it as sensitive. Changing it
# restarts today's unique visitor count, nothing more.
ANALYTICS_SALT=
